target: internal/record/record.go
verify: go test ./internal/record/ -count=1 -run 'TestDisclosureRefusesAnUnreadableRun'
expect: Disclosure returned
why:    a run whose record did not decode has no reviewable summary, and an EMPTY disclosure is not a safe default for one: the subcommand turns "" into a JSON null, which Step 14 reads as `converged, nothing owed`. So the one shape that must never render silently is exactly the shape a dropped error check renders.
--- old
	conv, err := r.Convergence()
	if err != nil {
		return "", err
	}
--- new
	conv, _ := r.Convergence()
